{"seconds": 40.8, "exit": 0, "final": "Wait, Qxc8 is actually check (the king is on e7 after Ke7). After Qxc8+ Qxc7, White is still up a rook (5 points).\n\nPerfect! The main line is: **Nc7+ Ke7 Qxc8+ Qxc7** and White is up a full rook.\n\n---\n\n## Coaching Note\n\nThe move **Nc7+** forks the king and rook. Your knight attacks e8 (check) and c8 simultaneously\u2014Black's king must move (Ke7 is forced), leaving the rook undefended. Then Qxc8 wins the rook outright. **Key lesson:** when you have two pieces attacking enemy squares, look for forcing moves (checks, captures) that hit multiple targets. If one target must move or can't defend the other, you win material.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Nc7+\", \"line\": [\"Nc7+\", \"Ke7\", \"Qxc8+\", \"Qxc7\", \"Nxc7\", \"Qxe5\"], \"motifs\": [\"fork\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "2rnkb1r/pQ3ppp/5n2/2qNN2b/2P1P3/3B3P/P2P1PP1/R3K2R w KQk - 2 15"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "2rnkb1r/pQ3ppp/5n2/2qNN2b/2P1P3/3B3P/P2P1PP1/R3K2R w KQk - 2 15"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2rnkb1r/pQ3ppp/5n2/2qNN2b/2P1P3/3B3P/P2P1PP1/R3K2R w KQk - 2 15", "square": "b7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2rnkb1r/pQ3ppp/5n2/2qNN2b/2P1P3/3B3P/P2P1PP1/R3K2R w KQk - 2 15", "square": "e5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2rnkb1r/pQ3ppp/5n2/2qNN2b/2P1P3/3B3P/P2P1PP1/R3K2R w KQk - 2 15", "square": "d5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-line_view", "args": {"fen": "2rnkb1r/pQ3ppp/5n2/2qNN2b/2P1P3/3B3P/P2P1PP1/R3K2R w KQk - 2 15", "square": "d3"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "2rnkb1r/pQ3ppp/5n2/2qNN2b/2P1P3/3B3P/P2P1PP1/R3K2R w KQk - 2 15"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2rnkb1r/pQ3ppp/5n2/2qNN2b/2P1P3/3B3P/P2P1PP1/R3K2R w KQk - 2 15", "move": "Nc7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "2rnkb1r/pQ3ppp/5n2/2qNN2b/2P1P3/3B3P/P2P1PP1/R